A||||5||Voytek||Fuel Pump Runs On -- Question||||1||
Z||000000||Voytek||08-28-2001||03:24 PM||||Ok.  Symptom: with the ignition off and key removed, the fuel pump keeps running until I remove the fuse ('87 GT)<P>I did the search and found some good info, like checking the relay behind the firewall.  Did that by swapping the relays and the problem is still there.<P>Someone said it can be the oil pressure switch.  This is where my question comes in.  Is this the same unit that controls the oil pressure gauge or is there a separate switch?<P>Thanks for any info.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-28-2001||03:41 PM||||Its the same unit. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-28-2001||04:04 PM||||Yup, <B>EASY FIX!</B> Its the oil pressure sending unit. (I had the same prob on my Formula). Cost around 20 bucks at Autozone. Take the battery out for easy access. 10 minute job tops! <P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||14
Z||000003||StuGood||08-28-2001||05:05 PM||||If you've got a stock GT, it's the same unit, as the others have posted.  The no-cost test is: Remove the connector from the oil pressure gage sending unit, by squeezing the ring and pulling the connector off.  When you plug the fuel pump fuse back in, the fuel pump should not run on.  The appropriate thing to say at this point is, "Aha!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Then you replace the sending unit.  ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Kasdan||08-28-2001||06:50 PM||||Funny, i had this same problem a few months ago if u guys remember.  Yep, check the sending unit.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||08-28-2001||08:30 PM||||Make sure there is a rubber grommet on the wire harness plug for "new" oil sending unit.  It keeps the water out of the sending unit.  water + wires + electricity = short ||||reg||1
